{"additional":"","additionalPlain":"","categories":{"commitment":"Full Time Remote","location":"Remote","team":"eDiscovery","allLocations":["Remote"]},"createdAt":1788463628037,"descriptionPlain":"eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager \nEmployment Type: Full Time, Mid-Level\nDepartment: eDiscovery\n \nCGS is seeking an eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager to join our team supporting the legal mission of a large state agency. The eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager oversees the daily operational and technical execution of litigation support services. They will assist the Program Manager in leading team personnel, refining workflows, and managing technology platforms. They will ensure that all electronic data collection, processing, hosting, review, and production deliverables meet stringent quality, timeline, and security requirements. \n \nCGS brings motivated, highly skilled, and creative people together to solve the government’s most dynamic problems with cutting-edge technology. To carry out our mission, we are seeking candidates who are excited to contribute to government innovation, appreciate collaboration, and can anticipate the needs of others. Here at CGS, we offer an environment in which our employees feel supported, and we encourage professional growth through various learning opportunities.\n \nKey Responsibilities \n· Operational Execution: Coordinate day-to-day operations of the eDiscovery team, including monitoring of priority tasks, deadline tracking, and maintaining accurate project trackers. \n· Technical Quality Assurance: Establish and enforce monitoring and quality control protocols for all phases of the EDRM encompassing data collection through production.\n· Team Supervision: Provide daily oversight, consultation, and support for eDiscovery project managers, data analysts, forensic analysts, and technical staff supporting the engagement.\n· Vendor & Tool Management: Coordinate with eDiscovery leads and vendors to ensure data management tools and environments (such as Relativity) are optimized for optimal performance.\n· Acting Leadership: Assume full management responsibilities for the eDiscovery program in the absence of the Program Manager.\n \nRequired Qualifications\n· Experience: 4+ years of hands-on experience in eDiscovery project management or litigation support operations.\n· Leadership: 1+ years of experience leading teams, supervising staff, or managing complex operational shifts.\n· Technical Expertise: Advanced proficiency in managing databases within Relativity or equivalent EDRM processing and review engines.\n· Problem Solving: Proven ability to troubleshoot critical database issues and database errors under tight court deadlines.\n· Knowledge Management: Experience managing and organizing information pertaining to large and complex litigations involving multiple cases, courts, jurisdictions, and plaintiffs.\nPreferred Certifications: \nCertified eDiscovery Specialist (CEDS), Relativity Certified Administrator (RCA), Project Management Professional (PMP), Program Management Professional (PgMP), Relativity Specialist (Project Management, Data Management, Analytics, Review Management)\n \nOur commitment:\n \nContact Government Services (CGS) strives to simplify and enhance government bureaucracy through the optimization of human, technical, and financial resources. We combine cutting edge technology with world-class personnel to deliver customized solutions that fit our clients’ specific needs. We are committed to solving the most challenging and dynamic problems. \n \nFor the past seven years we’ve been growing our government-contracting portfolio, and along the way we’ve created valuable partnerships by demonstrating a commitment to honesty, professionalism, and quality work.\nHere at CGS we value honesty through hard work and self-awareness, professionalism in all we do, and to deliver the best quality to our consumers mending those relations for years to come.\n \nWe care about our employees. Therefore, we offer a comprehensive benefits package:\n- Health, Dental, and Vision\n- Life Insurance\n- 401k\n- Flexible Spending Account (Health, Dependent Care, and Commuter)\n- Paid Time Off and Observance of State/Federal Holidays\n \nContact Government Services, LLC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants will be considered without regard to their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran.\nJoin our team and become part of meaningful government innovation!\nExplore additional job opportunities with CGS on our Job Board: \nhttps://cgsfederal.com/join-our-team/\nFor more information about CGS please visit: https://www.cgsfederal.com or contact:\nEmail: info@cgsfederal.com\n \n#CJ\n","description":"<div><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager </span></strong></div>\n<div>Employment Type: Full Time, Mid-Level</div>\n<div>Department: eDiscovery</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">CGS is seeking an eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager to join our team supporting the legal mission of a large state agency. The eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager oversees the daily operational and technical execution of litigation support services. They will assist the Program Manager in leading team personnel, refining workflows, and managing technology platforms. They will ensure that all electronic data collection, processing, hosting, review, and production deliverables meet stringent quality, timeline, and security requirements.&nbsp;</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">CGS brings motivated, highly skilled, and creative people together to solve the government’s most dynamic problems with cutting-edge technology. To carry out our mission, we are seeking candidates who are excited to contribute to government innovation, appreciate collaboration, and can anticipate the needs of others. Here at CGS, we offer an environment in which our employees feel supported, and we encourage professional growth through various learning opportunities.</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Key Responsibilities&nbsp;</span></strong></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">· <strong>Operational Execution: </strong>Coordinate day-to-day operations of the eDiscovery team, including monitoring of priority tasks, deadline tracking, and maintaining accurate project trackers.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>· <strong>Technical Quality Assurance:</strong> Establish and enforce monitoring and quality control protocols for all phases of the EDRM encompassing data collection through production.</p>\n<p>· <strong>Team Supervision:</strong> Provide daily oversight, consultation, and support for eDiscovery project managers, data analysts, forensic analysts, and technical staff supporting the engagement.</p>\n<p>· <strong>Vendor &amp; Tool Management:</strong> Coordinate with eDiscovery leads and vendors to ensure data management tools and environments (such as Relativity) are optimized for optimal performance.</p>\n<p>· <strong>Acting Leadership:</strong> Assume full management responsibilities for the eDiscovery program in the absence of the Program Manager.</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<h4><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></h4>\n<div>\n<p>· <strong>Experience: </strong>4+ years of hands-on experience in eDiscovery project management or litigation support operations.</p>\n<p>· <strong>Leadership:</strong> 1+ years of experience leading teams, supervising staff, or managing complex operational shifts.</p>\n<p>· <strong>Technical Expertise:</strong> Advanced proficiency in managing databases within Relativity or equivalent EDRM processing and review engines.</p>\n<p>· <strong>Problem Solving: </strong>Proven ability to troubleshoot critical database issues and database errors under tight court deadlines.</p>\n<p>· <strong>Knowledge Management:</strong> Experience managing and organizing information pertaining to large and complex litigations involving multiple cases, courts, jurisdictions, and plaintiffs.</p>\n<p><strong>Preferred Certifications:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>Certified eDiscovery Specialist (CEDS), Relativity Certified Administrator (RCA), Project Management Professional (PMP), Program Management Professional (PgMP), Relativity Specialist (Project Management, Data Management, Analytics, Review Management)</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>\n<div><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Our commitment:</span></strong></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Contact Government Services (CGS) strives to simplify and enhance government bureaucracy through the optimization of human, technical, and financial resources. We combine cutting edge technology with world-class personnel to deliver customized solutions that fit our clients’ specific needs. We are committed to solving the most challenging and dynamic problems. </span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">For the past seven years we’ve been growing our government-contracting portfolio, and along the way we’ve created valuable partnerships by demonstrating a commitment to honesty, professionalism, and quality work.</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Here at CGS we value honesty through hard work and self-awareness, professionalism in all we do, and to deliver the best quality to our consumers mending those relations for years to come.</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">We care about our employees. Therefore, we offer a comprehensive benefits package:</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Health, Dental, and Vision</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Life Insurance</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- 401k</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Flexible Spending Account (Health, Dependent Care, and Commuter)</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Paid Time Off and Observance of State/Federal Holidays</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Contact Government Services, LLC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants will be considered without regard to their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran.</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Join our team and become part of meaningful government innovation!</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Explore additional job opportunities with CGS on our Job Board: </span></div>\n<div><a href=\"https://cgsfederal.com/join-our-team/\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\" class=\"postings-link\">https://cgsfederal.com/join-our-team/</a></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">For more information about CGS please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.cgsfederal.com/\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\" class=\"postings-link\">https://www.cgsfederal.com</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> or contact:</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Email:&nbsp;</span><a href=\"mailto:info@cgsfederal.com\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\" class=\"postings-link\">info@cgsfederal.com</a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>#CJ</div>\n</div>\n</div>","id":"1ff0a19c-69de-4ed4-bf38-ab14b58a2591","lists":[],"salaryRange":{"min":150000,"max":175000,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-year-salary"},"text":"eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager","country":"US","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager </span></strong></div>\n<div>Employment Type: Full Time, Mid-Level</div>\n<div>Department: eDiscovery</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">CGS is seeking an eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager to join our team supporting the legal mission of a large state agency. The eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager oversees the daily operational and technical execution of litigation support services. They will assist the Program Manager in leading team personnel, refining workflows, and managing technology platforms. They will ensure that all electronic data collection, processing, hosting, review, and production deliverables meet stringent quality, timeline, and security requirements.&nbsp;</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">CGS brings motivated, highly skilled, and creative people together to solve the government&rsquo;s most dynamic problems with cutting-edge technology. To carry out our mission, we are seeking candidates who are excited to contribute to government innovation, appreciate collaboration, and can anticipate the needs of others. Here at CGS, we offer an environment in which our employees feel supported, and we encourage professional growth through various learning opportunities.</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Key Responsibilities&nbsp;</span></strong></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&middot; <strong>Operational Execution: </strong>Coordinate day-to-day operations of the eDiscovery team, including monitoring of priority tasks, deadline tracking, and maintaining accurate project trackers.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Technical Quality Assurance:</strong> Establish and enforce monitoring and quality control protocols for all phases of the EDRM encompassing data collection through production.</p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Team Supervision:</strong> Provide daily oversight, consultation, and support for eDiscovery project managers, data analysts, forensic analysts, and technical staff supporting the engagement.</p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Vendor &amp; Tool Management:</strong> Coordinate with eDiscovery leads and vendors to ensure data management tools and environments (such as Relativity) are optimized for optimal performance.</p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Acting Leadership:</strong> Assume full management responsibilities for the eDiscovery program in the absence of the Program Manager.</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<h4><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></h4>\n<div>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Experience: </strong>4+ years of hands-on experience in eDiscovery project management or litigation support operations.</p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Leadership:</strong> 1+ years of experience leading teams, supervising staff, or managing complex operational shifts.</p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Technical Expertise:</strong> Advanced proficiency in managing databases within Relativity or equivalent EDRM processing and review engines.</p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Problem Solving: </strong>Proven ability to troubleshoot critical database issues and database errors under tight court deadlines.</p>\n<p>&middot; <strong>Knowledge Management:</strong> Experience managing and organizing information pertaining to large and complex litigations involving multiple cases, courts, jurisdictions, and plaintiffs.</p>\n<p><strong>Preferred Certifications:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>Certified eDiscovery Specialist (CEDS), Relativity Certified Administrator (RCA), Project Management Professional (PMP), Program Management Professional (PgMP), Relativity Specialist (Project Management, Data Management, Analytics, Review Management)</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>\n<div><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Our commitment:</span></strong></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Contact Government Services (CGS) strives to simplify and enhance government bureaucracy through the optimization of human, technical, and financial resources. We combine cutting edge technology with world-class personnel to deliver customized solutions that fit our clients&rsquo; specific needs. We are committed to solving the most challenging and dynamic problems. </span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">For the past seven years we&rsquo;ve been growing our government-contracting portfolio, and along the way we&rsquo;ve created valuable partnerships by demonstrating a commitment to honesty, professionalism, and quality work.</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Here at CGS we value honesty through hard work and self-awareness, professionalism in all we do, and to deliver the best quality to our consumers mending those relations for years to come.</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">We care about our employees. Therefore, we offer a comprehensive benefits package:</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Health, Dental, and Vision</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Life Insurance</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- 401k</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Flexible Spending Account (Health, Dependent Care, and Commuter)</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">- Paid Time Off and Observance of State/Federal Holidays</span></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Contact Government Services, LLC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants will be considered without regard to their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran.</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Join our team and become part of meaningful government innovation!</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Explore additional job opportunities with CGS on our Job Board: </span></div>\n<div><a class=\"postings-link\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\" href=\"https://cgsfederal.com/join-our-team/\">https://cgsfederal.com/join-our-team/</a></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">For more information about CGS please visit: </span><a class=\"postings-link\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\" href=\"https://www.cgsfederal.com/\">https://www.cgsfederal.com</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> or contact:</span></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Email:&nbsp;</span><a class=\"postings-link\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\" href=\"mailto:info@cgsfederal.com\">info@cgsfederal.com</a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>#CJ</div>\n</div>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager \nEmployment Type: Full Time, Mid-Level\nDepartment: eDiscovery\n \nCGS is seeking an eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager to join our team supporting the legal mission of a large state agency. The eDiscovery Deputy Program Manager oversees the daily operational and technical execution of litigation support services. They will assist the Program Manager in leading team personnel, refining workflows, and managing technology platforms. They will ensure that all electronic data collection, processing, hosting, review, and production deliverables meet stringent quality, timeline, and security requirements. \n \nCGS brings motivated, highly skilled, and creative people together to solve the government’s most dynamic problems with cutting-edge technology. To carry out our mission, we are seeking candidates who are excited to contribute to government innovation, appreciate collaboration, and can anticipate the needs of others. Here at CGS, we offer an environment in which our employees feel supported, and we encourage professional growth through various learning opportunities.\n \nKey Responsibilities \n· Operational Execution: Coordinate day-to-day operations of the eDiscovery team, including monitoring of priority tasks, deadline tracking, and maintaining accurate project trackers. \n· Technical Quality Assurance: Establish and enforce monitoring and quality control protocols for all phases of the EDRM encompassing data collection through production.\n· Team Supervision: Provide daily oversight, consultation, and support for eDiscovery project managers, data analysts, forensic analysts, and technical staff supporting the engagement.\n· Vendor & Tool Management: Coordinate with eDiscovery leads and vendors to ensure data management tools and environments (such as Relativity) are optimized for optimal performance.\n· Acting Leadership: Assume full management responsibilities for the eDiscovery program in the absence of the Program Manager.\n \nRequired Qualifications\n· Experience: 4+ years of hands-on experience in eDiscovery project management or litigation support operations.\n· Leadership: 1+ years of experience leading teams, supervising staff, or managing complex operational shifts.\n· Technical Expertise: Advanced proficiency in managing databases within Relativity or equivalent EDRM processing and review engines.\n· Problem Solving: Proven ability to troubleshoot critical database issues and database errors under tight court deadlines.\n· Knowledge Management: Experience managing and organizing information pertaining to large and complex litigations involving multiple cases, courts, jurisdictions, and plaintiffs.\nPreferred Certifications: \nCertified eDiscovery Specialist (CEDS), Relativity Certified Administrator (RCA), Project Management Professional (PMP), Program Management Professional (PgMP), Relativity Specialist (Project Management, Data Management, Analytics, Review Management)\n \nOur commitment:\n \nContact Government Services (CGS) strives to simplify and enhance government bureaucracy through the optimization of human, technical, and financial resources. We combine cutting edge technology with world-class personnel to deliver customized solutions that fit our clients’ specific needs. We are committed to solving the most challenging and dynamic problems. \n \nFor the past seven years we’ve been growing our government-contracting portfolio, and along the way we’ve created valuable partnerships by demonstrating a commitment to honesty, professionalism, and quality work.\nHere at CGS we value honesty through hard work and self-awareness, professionalism in all we do, and to deliver the best quality to our consumers mending those relations for years to come.\n \nWe care about our employees. Therefore, we offer a comprehensive benefits package:\n- Health, Dental, and Vision\n- Life Insurance\n- 401k\n- Flexible Spending Account (Health, Dependent Care, and Commuter)\n- Paid Time Off and Observance of State/Federal Holidays\n \nContact Government Services, LLC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants will be considered without regard to their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran.\nJoin our team and become part of meaningful government innovation!\nExplore additional job opportunities with CGS on our Job Board: \nhttps://cgsfederal.com/join-our-team/\nFor more information about CGS please visit: https://www.cgsfederal.com or contact:\nEmail: info@cgsfederal.com\n \n#CJ\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/cgsfederal/1ff0a19c-69de-4ed4-bf38-ab14b58a2591","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/cgsfederal/1ff0a19c-69de-4ed4-bf38-ab14b58a2591/apply"}